The types CheckpointEntry and AofSyncTaskInfo are inaccessible due to protection level, and ReplicaSyncSession is internal sealed partial class with a primary constructor, so it is not accessible outside the assembly. Also, the method AcquireCheckpointEntryAsync is private or internal, so I cannot call it directly in a test.

The best approach is to test the public method SendCheckpointAsync which calls AcquireCheckpointEntryAsync internally and logs the information on iteration. This will indirectly cover the logging call on line 361.

I will write a test for SendCheckpointAsync that verifies the logger.LogInformation call with the expected message.

I will submit the test now. It will mock dependencies and verify the logger call. I will not try to call AcquireCheckpointEntryAsync directly since it is inaccessible.

